##  AI-Powered Student Support System

An end-to-end Machine Learning dashboard that identifies **at-risk students**, explains predictions using **Explainable AI (SHAP)**, analyzes student feedback sentiment, and provides **personalized academic recommendations** through an interactive Streamlit web application.

This system helps educational institutions detect struggling students early and take proactive intervention.

## Live Demo

Access the deployed system:

https://yonashabtamucom-ai-student-dashboard-student-dashboard-ukscdt.streamlit.app/

## Project Objectives

The main objectives of this project are:

• Predict students at risk of low academic performance
• Explain predictions using Explainable AI (SHAP)
• Provide personalized recommendations
• Analyze student feedback sentiment using NLP
• Provide role-based secure dashboard access
• Deploy the system online

## Features

## 1. Secure Login System

* Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
* Admin, Instructor, and Student roles
* Password hashing using bcrypt
* SQLite database authentication

## 2. Dashboard Overview

* Total student count
* At-risk student count
* Model accuracy
* Student distribution visualization

## 3. At-Risk Student Prediction

* Random Forest Classifier
* Identifies low-performance students
* Displays confusion matrix and performance metrics

## 4. Explainable AI (SHAP)

* Explains why a student is at risk
* Shows feature importance per student
* Provides transparent AI decisions

## 5. Performance Score Prediction

* Random Forest Regressor
* Predicts engagement-based performance score
* Shows MAE and R² score

## 6. Feedback Sentiment Analysis

* NLP using TextBlob
* Detects positive and negative student feedback
* Visual sentiment distribution

## 7. Personalized Recommendations

Provides suggestions based on:

* Attendance
* Participation
* Engagement level
* Parent involvement

## 8. Academic Chatbot

* Rule-based chatbot assistant
* Answers student performance questions

##  Machine Learning Models

## Classification Model

Model: Random Forest Classifier
Purpose: Predict at-risk students

Performance:
Accuracy: 95%
Precision: 95%
Recall: 94%

## Regression Model

Model: Random Forest Regressor
Purpose: Predict student performance score

Performance:

MAE: 0.29
R² Score: 0.69

## Dataset

Dataset: xAPI-Edu-Data.csv

Contains:

• Student participation
• Attendance records
• Resource usage
• Academic performance

Total records: 480 students

Target variable:

at_risk
0 = Safe student
1 = At-risk student
## System Architecture

Dataset
↓
Data Preprocessing
↓
Machine Learning Models
↓
Explainable AI (SHAP)
↓
